@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP ProjectForge. Basic Git/issue/board behavior belongs to separate ProjectForge, with independent user/resource authority.
allowmixing
title AFTER MVP — advanced model — Proposed / illustrative — Repository and collaboration identity model
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class RepositoryRecord
class RefObservation <<branch / tag name and observed object>>
class NativeCommit <<backend-owned identity>>
class PullRequestContext
class ReviewEvidence
class CheckEvidence
class RepositoryMutationAttempt
class UserContext <<Identity-owned current context>>
class Team <<optional grouping, no grant allocated>>
RepositoryRecord --> RefObservation
RefObservation --> NativeCommit : branch tip in selected example
PullRequestContext --> RepositoryRecord : exact source / target
PullRequestContext --> NativeCommit : evaluated revisions
PullRequestContext --> ReviewEvidence
PullRequestContext --> CheckEvidence
RepositoryMutationAttempt --> PullRequestContext : attributable merge intent
ReviewEvidence --> UserContext : actor identity / actual review scope
Team ..> UserContext : only if actual team model adopted

@enduml
